<title>CHINA: China sets bonded oil depot on Hainan.</title>
<headline>China sets bonded oil depot on Hainan.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>China has set up a 30 million yuan bonded oil depot on the southern island of Hainan, the official Xinhua news agency said.</p>
<p>The depot was set up by the Hainan Ruiyin Fuel and Chemicals Co Ltd to provide oil for international cargo ships and fishing vessels, Xinhua said in a report issued late on Thursday.</p>
<p>Hainan is considered to be a special economic zone, allowing it more flexibility in setting economic policies.</p>
</text>
